<!--
    The app's mark — a domino mask — as a 24dp glyph. It used to be an envelope,
    which read as "something to do with mail" in the Quick Settings tile picker
    and shared nothing with the icon the user taps on their home screen.

    The path is the shipped launcher art (drawable-*/ic_launcher_monochrome.png)
    measured and re-drawn as curves: the outer silhouette and both eye holes land
    within a few percent of the raster, so tile and launcher show one silhouette.

    WHITE ON PURPOSE, and only for the surfaces that tint it themselves:
      - the Quick Settings tile, where SystemUI applies its own on/off tint,
      - notification small icons and actions, which the platform flattens to a
        monochrome mask anyway.
    The launcher shortcut does NOT tint, and white is invisible there against the
    white circle Launcher3 wraps a legacy icon in — that is the bug this file
    used to cause. The shortcut is served by ic_shortcut_quick_mask.xml instead,
    which carries its own background.
-->
